[[Zhalia Moon]] used Venomhand in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], almost killing [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] before she came to her senses. [[Klaus]] later used the spell against [[Dante Vale]], overpowering his [[Dragonfist]] spell. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

Zhalia tried to use the spell against [[Chemosh]] but he knocked her to the ground before she could use it. {{source|To Be Together}}

Zhalia used the spell to attack [[Araknos]] during the Huntik team's final battle against [[the Professor]]. It proved ineffective however as Araknos was still able to fire his spider silk. {{Source|The Mission}}

[[Wilder]] threatened to use Venomhand against a weakened Sophie to finish her off, until Lok stopped him with the [[Willblade]]. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

Zhalia used the spell as "weedkiller" to free herself from [[Wildwood Druid]]'s roots. {{source|Chasing Void}}

[[Stack]] tried to hit [[Shauna]] with Venomhand in [[Klaus' bookshop]], but she easily dodged it. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

Zhalia used the spell to attack [[Tantras]] on the [[Erasmus Bridge]]. {{Source|Den vs Harrison}}

Tantras used Venomhand to murder [[Stack]] in the [[Blood Spiral Base]], teaching his students what the [[Blood Spiral]] does to spies. {{source|Boys Will Be Seekers}} 

In the [[Great Rift Valley, Africa|Great Rift Valley]], Tantras tried to do the same to Zhalia after discovering her true identity, but he was stopped by her [[Powerbond|powerbonding]] with [[Gareon]] and the pair subsequently erasing his memory. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

On the island of the [[Phoenix]], a [[Casterwill Hunter]] attempted to use the spell on [[Montehue]] after jumping him from behind, but he grabbed her arm and fell backwards onto her, crushing her. {{Source|S2E44}} In the [[Phoenix Volcano]], [[Shauna]] used [[Doublespell]] combined with Venomhand while running to attack Lok, but she was interrupted by Sophie. She later used the spell to try and finish off a captive Sophie, who dodged it. {{source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

In [[the Professor's castle]], Wilder attempted to finish off [[Den Fears]] with the spell but was interrupted by [[Grier]]. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}

{{clear}}

